# LLP 0013 Hermes patch 0014 — one-way dynamic-code latch and fast-path gate
# Class: C (small upstream correctness/security fix plus narrow embedder latch).
# @ref LLP 0013#patch-shape-discipline — narrow backportable flag enforcement.
#
# Hermes's Function constructor recognizes `return this` (including whitespace
# variants) and returns a cached code block before directEval checks
# Runtime::enableEval. A runtime created with eval disabled can therefore still
# recover globalThis through Function, constructor walks, or Reflect. Gate that
# fast path on the same runtime flag.
#
# Ibex's trusted bootstrap itself currently needs Function, so RuntimeConfig
# cannot close compilation from construction time. The exported one-way latch
# lets an embedder finish trusted bootstrap and then irreversibly clear
# Runtime::enableEval before application code. Host evaluateJavaScript remains
# available for the preselected bundle; there is deliberately no re-enable API.

